-- Replace reused interview options with specific, varied dialogue (part 2).
WITH tailored(question_text, a,b,c,d) AS (VALUES
('Do you already know what the next era of the band sounds like?', 'We have a few new sounds we''re excited to explore.', 'We''re experimenting, but nothing is fixed yet.', 'Expect something heavier and stranger than the last record.', 'Ask me after we''ve survived the next rehearsal.'),
('Do you see the band staying together indefinitely?', 'I''d love us to keep making music as long as we''re happy.', 'We take each chapter as it comes.', 'We''ll stop when we''ve genuinely run out of things to say.', 'Indefinitely? Have you ever lived on a tour bus?'),
('Is there a genre you''d like to explore next?', 'I''d love to bring more electronic textures into our songs.', 'We might borrow from jazz or folk without changing who we are.', 'A full-on industrial record would surprise a few people.', 'Polka, just to confuse the algorithm.'),
('Is there an artist you desperately want to collaborate with?', 'Someone whose songwriting pushes us in a new direction.', 'We look for chemistry more than famous names.', 'Give us an unpredictable collaborator and let us make noise.', 'Anyone who brings their own studio snacks.'),
('What venue do you dream of headlining?', 'A packed stadium singing every chorus would be incredible.', 'A historic theatre with amazing acoustics is on my list.', 'A massive festival main stage at midnight.', 'Anywhere with a working backstage kettle.'),
('What would make you feel you''d achieved everything you wanted?', 'Hearing our music still matter to people years later.', 'Making records we love without worrying about survival.', 'Selling out a world tour on our own terms.', 'A day off when nobody sends me a spreadsheet.'),
('Where do you want the band to be in five years?', 'Still creating music and playing bigger stages together.', 'Making a living from records and shows would be a victory.', 'Headlining arenas and redefining our sound.', 'With a tour bus that doesn''t leak.'),
('Would you ever make a concept album?', 'Absolutely; I love stories that unfold across a whole record.', 'If the songs support one theme, we''d consider it.', 'A strange interconnected album could be our boldest move.', 'Only if the concept isn''t about our van breaking down.'),
('Would you ever score a film or game?', 'I''d love to write music that builds a whole fictional world.', 'It could work if the story suits our sound.', 'Give us a dark game soundtrack and a full orchestra.', 'Yes, especially if my character gets a guitar solo.'),
('Would you ever take a long break at your commercial peak?', 'If we needed rest, protecting the band comes first.', 'We''d plan a pause rather than disappear without explanation.', 'Walking away at the top could be the bravest decision.', 'Peak or not, I''m sleeping for a month.'),
('Do clothes and visual style matter as much as the songs?', 'The music comes first, but visuals help tell its story.', 'Clothes and artwork should fit the sound rather than distract.', 'An unforgettable image can hit as hard as a riff.', 'Our wardrobe can''t rescue a terrible chorus.'),
('Do you care whether people think you''re cool?', 'I''d rather be genuine than chase anyone''s approval.', 'It''s nice to be admired, but it isn''t the goal.', 'Trying to look cool is usually the least cool thing.', 'I lost that battle the day I bought stage boots.'),
('Do you think rock music takes itself too seriously?', 'Sometimes; making music should still be fun.', 'There''s space for ambition and a sense of humour.', 'Too many bands forget that danger can be playful.', 'Some guitar solos could use a joke break.'),
('Has your public persona become different from who you are privately?', 'The stage amplifies part of me, but it isn''t a disguise.', 'I keep some parts of my life just for myself.', 'Fans see the fearless version, not the tired person afterwards.', 'Offstage I''m mostly hunting for a quiet chair.'),
('Have you ever felt pressured to change how you look?', 'Yes, but I''ve learned to trust what feels comfortable.', 'We''ve heard advice and decided what fits our identity.', 'No stylist gets to decide whether I belong on stage.', 'They asked for subtle; I bought more glitter.'),
('How carefully planned is the band''s image?', 'We choose artwork and clothes that reflect each release.', 'Some visuals are planned; the best moments happen naturally.', 'We shape the image as deliberately as the sound.', 'The plan ends when someone spills coffee on the outfits.'),
('How important is mystery for an artist?', 'Leaving something unsaid can make a song more intriguing.', 'We share enough to connect without opening every door.', 'A little mystique beats posting every meal online.', 'Our biggest mystery is where the spare cables go.'),
('How much thought goes into artwork and visual identity?', 'We spend ages connecting colours and imagery to the songs.', 'The artwork grows alongside the music, not after it.', 'A striking cover can define an entire era.', 'More thought than goes into packing the merch box.'),
('Is authenticity possible once a band becomes a brand?', 'Yes, if decisions still begin with the music.', 'Commercial success doesn''t have to erase personal values.', 'The danger starts when the logo matters more than the songs.', 'We''ll worry when our accountant joins the songwriting team.'),
('Would you ever completely reinvent the band''s image?', 'Yes, if our music genuinely takes a new direction.', 'I''d change the visuals gradually so fans can follow us.', 'A total reinvention could shake us out of a rut.', 'Next album, everybody wears identical silver helmets.'),
('Are festivals giving enough opportunities to new bands?', 'Not yet; emerging artists need decent slots and pay.', 'Some festivals are improving, but access varies widely.', 'Headliners should help open doors for the next generation.', 'Put new bands on before the audience goes home.'),
('Do artists need to become content creators to survive?', 'Musicians should be able to focus on making music.', 'Online content helps, but it shouldn''t replace touring or recordings.', 'I''d rather make a memorable album than fifty daily clips.', 'I''m a songwriter, not a full-time ring light.'),
('Do playlists have too much influence over what becomes successful?', 'Discovery playlists help, but can narrow what gets heard.', 'They should be one route to fans, not the only route.', 'One curator shouldn''t decide a band''s future.', 'My playlist keeps recommending songs from our rivals.'),
('Do record labels still have too much power?', 'Artists deserve more say over rights and releases.', 'The best labels work as partners, not gatekeepers.', 'Some contracts still look like a trap with better stationery.', 'I''d read the small print before signing anything.'),
('Has streaming made the music industry better or worse?', 'It helps fans discover us, but payments need improving.', 'Access is better while the economics remain complicated.', 'A million plays should mean more than a tiny cheque.', 'Great for listeners; less great for our petrol budget.'),
('Is it harder for guitar bands to break through now?', 'It''s crowded, but a strong live band can still stand out.', 'The routes have changed; guitar music hasn''t vanished.', 'A loud riff can cut through any trend.', 'Tell that to the crowd in front of our amps.'),
('Is social media now more important than radio?', 'Social platforms reach fans quickly, but radio still matters.', 'They serve different audiences and can work together.', 'One viral clip can beat months of traditional promotion.', 'I''ll celebrate any station brave enough to play our whole song.'),
('Is the album format still important?', 'Absolutely; an album lets you build a bigger story.', 'Singles attract attention, while albums reward deeper listening.', 'I''d rather make a great record than chase twelve algorithms.', 'Yes; where else would we hide the weird track?'),
('Should chart rules change to reflect how people actually listen?', 'Charts should fairly represent genuine listening habits.', 'Changes make sense if they stay transparent and consistent.', 'Stop rewarding tricks that inflate numbers without real fans.', 'Just don''t invent a chart for toaster plays.'),
('What''s one thing you would change about the music industry tomorrow?', 'I''d make music careers more sustainable for new artists.', 'Fairer contracts and clearer royalty reporting would help.', 'I''d tear up the worst exploitative deals first.', 'I''d make every promoter provide actual hot food.'),
('Can influence ever become copying?', 'Yes, when admiration replaces your own creative choices.', 'Borrowing ideas is natural; originality lies in reshaping them.', 'If the hook is identical, calling it homage won''t save it.', 'Ask our lawyer before playing the reference track.'),
('Do you deliberately avoid listening to similar bands while writing?', 'Sometimes I take a break so our ideas stay fresh.', 'We still listen widely, but avoid chasing current trends.', 'I want to compete with our own previous record.', 'I tried silence once; it made the van unbearable.'),
('Do you worry about sounding too much like your heroes?', 'I honour their influence while finding our voice.', 'We test ideas that sound too familiar and adjust them.', 'I''d rather sound unmistakably us than perfectly like them.', 'If I start dressing like my idol, intervene.'),
('Has your taste changed since you started the band?', 'Definitely; touring exposed me to sounds I used to ignore.', 'I still love the old favourites alongside newer influences.', 'The older I get, the stranger my record collection becomes.', 'Yes, I even tolerate the bassist''s playlists now.'),
('Is there an influence in your music that fans usually miss?', 'There''s more film music in our arrangements than people realise.', 'Some rhythms come from music outside rock entirely.', 'Our quietest influences shape our loudest moments.', 'Nobody expects how much we love old game soundtracks.'),
('What album taught you the most about making music?', 'A raw live record taught me to value honest performances.', 'A carefully layered studio album showed me arrangement matters.', 'A fearless experimental record made me rewrite our approach.', 'An album with terrible mixing taught me what to avoid.'),
('What non-musical influence shapes your sound most?', 'The places we visit on tour end up in our lyrics.', 'Films, books and conversations all feed into our songs.', 'Anger at everyday injustices gives some tracks their edge.', 'Mostly the weather outside the rehearsal room.'),
('Which artist had the biggest influence on you growing up?', 'A fearless singer taught me to tell the truth in songs.', 'I drew different lessons from several great bands.', 'The loudest band I could find made me pick up an instrument.', 'Whoever annoyed my parents the most.'),
('Which artist would surprise people to learn you love?', 'I have a soft spot for beautifully written pop songs.', 'I listen to classical composers for their arrangements.', 'Some of my favourite music has no guitars at all.', 'I know every word to a ridiculous novelty hit.'),
('Which era of music would you most like to have been part of?', 'The early punk era had an incredible creative spark.', 'I''d love to witness the rise of stadium rock firsthand.', 'The experimental late seventies would suit us perfectly.', 'Any era with better tour-bus beds.'),
('Could the band continue if a key member left?', 'We''d take time to decide what feels right for everyone.', 'A change would reshape the sound, but might not end us.', 'No one is irreplaceable, even if it would hurt.', 'I''d at least need a week to learn their parts.'),
('Do you care about being inducted into halls of fame?', 'Recognition would be lovely, but it isn''t why we play.', 'If it happens, I''d be grateful for the people who got us there.', 'I''d rather fill venues than collect plaques.', 'Depends whether the statue gets my hair right.'),
('Do you think about your legacy while making new music?', 'I focus on writing songs that matter now.', 'Occasionally I wonder which tracks people will revisit.', 'I want records that outlive every passing trend.', 'I''m still trying to survive next week''s rehearsal.'),
('How do you want this band to be remembered?', 'As a band that made people feel less alone.', 'For memorable shows and records we believed in.', 'As the group that refused to play safe.', 'Preferably not for the broken backstage furniture.'),
('What part of your career do you think history might misunderstand?', 'People may miss how much work went into the early years.', 'Headlines rarely show the choices behind each record.', 'They''ll call our risks luck when they were deliberate.', 'They''ll think that haircut was a statement.'),
('What would make you proudest looking back on your career?', 'Knowing our music helped someone through a difficult time.', 'Having made a living without losing our friendships.', 'Creating a record nobody could mistake for another band.', 'Remembering every venue we actually played.'),
('Which song would you want people to still play in twenty years?', 'The one that means the most to our earliest fans.', 'A song whose lyrics still feel true decades later.', 'Our boldest track, not necessarily our biggest hit.', 'Whichever one finally pays for a holiday.'),
('Would you ever approve a documentary that showed the ugly parts too?', 'Yes, if it was fair to everyone involved.', 'I''d want honesty without exploiting private moments.', 'The messy parts are often the most important story.', 'Only after someone edits out my worst dancing.'),
('Would you rather burn brightly for five years or stay successful for thirty?', 'Thirty years making good music sounds extraordinary.', 'I''d choose a sustainable career over a quick peak.', 'Five explosive years could leave a bigger mark than thirty safe ones.', 'Can I choose five years and thirty holidays?'),
('Would you rather influence musicians or sell more records?', 'Inspiring another musician would mean a great deal.', 'I hope we can make an impact and still pay the bills.', 'I''d trade chart numbers for a sound others build on.', 'Ask again when the tour invoices arrive.')
)
UPDATE public.interview_questions AS q SET option_a_text=t.a,option_b_text=t.b,option_c_text=t.c,option_d_text=t.d
FROM tailored AS t WHERE q.question_text=t.question_text AND q.created_at::date=DATE '2026-09-02';